0214: 6-bit blend resolves without the target copy for cleared passes

The single-sample RGBA6 resolve (0176) copies the whole color target into a scratch texture and
quantizes it back: two full-screen reads and writes per resolved pass (Luigi's Mansion resolves
6-7 EFB passes per frame; at 3840x2160 the copies alone were ~0.7 ms of GPU time). A pass that
clears its color completely and will be resolved now renders into the scratch itself, and its
resolve quantizes the scratch straight into the target: the copy is gone for every cleared pass
(the main 3D view and the other full-clear passes). Peek-probe passes and multisampled targets are
unchanged; a resolve deferred by 0212 keeps track of where the pixels are. Byte-identical.
AURORA_EFB_BLEND6_NOREDIRECT=1: always copy (A/B).

